    <bpmn:process id="W_W4482" name="W4482. Item Auto-ID Data Model (GTIN, Serial, Lot/Batch, Expiry, Variable-Measure)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New regulated/perishable/serial SKU; traceability requirement
Frequency: Per onboarding + on regulation change
Volume: Regulated (DTI-BPS) + DG + lot-controlled SKUs (subset of 35K)
Owner: Auto-ID Lead / Master Data (VS-29)
Participants: Quality (VS-31), Recall (VS-89), DG (VS-114), DC (VS-04)
Source: workflow W4482 — Item Auto-ID Data Model (GTIN, Serial, Lot/Batch, Expiry, Variable-Measure)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4482_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4482_Lane1" name="Auto-ID Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4482_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4482_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4482_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4482_Lane2" name="Quality">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4482_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4482_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4482_Start4" name="New regulated/perishable/serial SKU; traceability requirement">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4482_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4482_Task5" name="Auto-ID Lead defines which attributes ride on the identifier — serial (power…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Auto-ID Lead defines which attributes ride on the identifier — serial (power tools, appliances), lot/batch (paint/chemical, cement), expiry (limited), and variable-measure (catch-weight lumber/wire/nails) per item type (profile §6.4)
Responsible (R): Auto-ID Lead / Quality
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: Per onboarding</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4482_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4482_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4482_Task6" name="Auto-ID Lead maps the data model to GS1-128 application identifiers and 2D (GS1…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Auto-ID Lead maps the data model to GS1-128 application identifiers and 2D (GS1 DataMatrix / QR) for dense data (lot+expiry+serial), and to the catch-weight/random-weight barcode format (links to VS-08/W115)
Responsible (R): Auto-ID Lead / IT
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: Per onboarding</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4482_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4482_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4482_Task7" name="Quality/Recall confirm the model supports recall traceability (VS-89) and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quality/Recall confirm the model supports recall traceability (VS-89) and DG/SDS access (VS-114); DC confirms lot/serial capture at receipt (VS-04)
Responsible (R): Quality / Recall / DC
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: Per onboarding</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4482_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4482_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4482_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4482_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-150 (ensure labeling &amp; Auto-ID data integrity.) | - CTL-683: lot/serial mandatory on regulated/DG items (VS-89/VS-114); catch-weight format validated; recall-traceability verified
Owner: Auto-ID Lead / Master Data (VS-29)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4482_Assoc10" sourceRef="W4482_Annotation9" targetRef="W4482_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
